# TF2's stock Flame Thrower's sounds (specs/tf2/effects.md 14.2): which
# start, loop, end and pilot-light sounds play, at what volume, and when
# each starts and stops, for a tap (15 ticks, 0.225 s), a 1 s (67 ticks)
# and a 6 s (400 ticks) burst, in the Pyro's own view (the local player,
# the stock Flame Thrower 21 swapped in: the account's Pyro carries the
# Dragon's Fury), plus a holster and redeploy. Two records:
# `sv_soundemitter_trace 1` prints every EmitSound / StopSound to
# tf/console.log (-condebug), placed by a marker `echo ft_t<n>` every 5
# ticks; `snd_show 1` draws every playing channel (volume 0-255, time
# left, looped) over the frame, photographed by the `snap`s
# `ft_<tick>` (read with tesseract). `host_framerate 0.015` makes each
# frame one tick; `wait 2` is one frame here. `givecurrentammo` before
# each burst (the 6 s burst runs dry otherwise). Generated.
#   tools/tf2ref/tf2ref.py scene tools/tf2ref/scenes/flame_sounds.tf2 --out <dir>
mp_disable_respawn_times 1
tf_weapon_criticals 0
host_framerate 0
bot_kick all
player red pyro
